            "result_text": "Done! I've saved the regex to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nThe regex works as follows:\n\n- **`(?=.*\\bIPv4\\b)`**: Lookahead asserting the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n- **`.*\\b`**: Matches everything up to a word boundary before the last date\n- **`(DATE_PATTERN)`**: Captured group for the date, with three alternatives for different month/day combinations\n- **`\\b(?!.*\\bDATE\\b)$`**: Ensures the captured date is the last one in the line (via negative lookahead) and is at line end\n\nThe regex correctly:\n- Rejects IPv4s with leading zeros (e.g., 192.168.001.1)\n- Validates month/day combinations (Feb ≤ 29, Apr/Jun/Sep/Nov ≤ 30, others ≤ 31)\n- Uses word boundaries to avoid matching numbers embedded in text\n- Captures only the last date when multiple dates exist in a line"
